            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">A 41-year-old female with 90 minutes of severe chest pain and ST-elevation in leads V1-V2 underwent emergency coronary angiography with a view to primary angioplasty.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INVESTIGATIONS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Physical examination, electrocardiography, coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DIAGNOSIS" NlmCategory="METHODS">ST-segment elevation anterior myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MANAGEMENT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Coronary angiography, antiplatelet and antithrombotic therapy, statin, angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor, beta blocker, IVUS and percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI)</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
